{"reference":"Jeremiah 33","book":"Jeremiah","chapter":33,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Restoration without denying loss","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Jeremiah 33 belongs to the restoration sequence in chapters 30–33, where healing and return are joined with rebuilding, replanting, forgiveness, and Davidic hope. The chapter’s promises of renewed joy, restored flocks, secure dwelling, and continuing royal and priestly service are therefore not presented as a denial of the devastation already described. They portray restoration as addressing a loss that remains fully in view.","verse_refs":["Jeremiah 33:1-26"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_jeremiah_033_3287eeb07899a229b2a28c15"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}